    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d139-a2">

                <pb facs="0307" n="211" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg211"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 2845.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Copy of proclamation.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Joh Teh Hu Ling, Magistrate</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            ana="#date_conversion-issue-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="chinese-era chinese-lunisolar"
                            notAfter="1897-12-15T23:59:59+08:05"
                            notBefore="1897-11-01T00:00:00+08:05"><hi rendition="#italic">15th 10
                                Moon Kwansu, 23d Year</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Notification is hereby given to notify all nations’ missionaries who are going
                    inland to rent houses or ground. I have had a dispatch from the Emperor stating
                    that it is legal, according to the treaty, to rent houses or ground, and also I
                    had a dispatch from the viceroy instructing me to protect all missionaries
                    coining to my district.</p>
                <p>There are two American missionaries, Mr. “Kiang A Teh,” “Be Liang Jing,” who have
                    rented a house outside of the west gate, and have made a written agreement for
                    the house; therefore I have sent my proclamation around, instructing and
                    prohibiting my subjects from troubling them in any way.</p>
            </div>
